  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of copper sulphate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is dissolved in deionised water to make <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of solution. The concentration of the copper sulphate solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&#160;mol&#160;</mtext><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;[</mo><mtext>Atomic masses&#160;</mtext><mi>Cu</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>32</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
